  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0: Retargeted from netstandard2.1 to netstandard2.0 (tracks\nUniversal.Common.Formats.Sfnt's own retarget) for broader consumer compatibility. Added 'glyf'/\n'loca' glyph outline parsing (simple and composite glyphs), 'kern' table (format 0), 'OS/2' table,\nand 'cvt '/'fpgm'/'prep' raw hinting-bytecode table reading (consumed by\nUniversal.Common.Formats.TrueType.Hinting). Added TrueType Collection (.ttc) support, reading the\nfirst font in the collection. Fixed two pre-existing bugs found while verifying the new outline\nparsing against real fonts: (1) HorizontalMetrics.Metrics had a Column-order collision (AdvanceWidth\nand LeftSideBearing were both declared at Order 0), making LeftSideBearing's parsed value depend on\nunspecified reflection member ordering instead of always reading correctly; (2)\nCharacterMap.SubtableFormat4.Map()'s idRangeOffset branch indexed GlyphIndexArray with a raw\nbyte-pointer-arithmetic offset instead of correcting it to an array index (missing the /2 and the\nsegment-position adjustment), silently returning an unrelated glyph for any codepoint whose cmap\nsegment uses the indirect form - this affected real accented Latin characters (e.g. Arial's 'é'\nresolved to an unrelated glyph, not an accented 'e', prior to this fix).",
